or":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097455,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc0NTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:web","name":"platform:web","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097780,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc3ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:macos","name":"platform:macos","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-07-15T04:55:47Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T20:32:10Z","closed_at":"2025-07-17T20:31:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nI narrowed it down to the release number with the web editor.\nWorking in 4.1.4.stable\nBroken in 4.2.dev1\n\nI could not get it to compile when trying to bisect it further due to some embree incompatibility with my version of clang or something. I can build it on my Windows machine then test it on my macbook to narrow it down to the commit if that would help.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.2.dev1 - Web - GLES3 (Compatibility) - WebKit WebGL -  (2 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nMipmaps for screen textures appear to be broken in web exports specifically on MacOS. It works fine on Windows. I haven't tested it on linux.\nBy broken, I mean `textureLod()` in the shader returns `0`s resulting in a black rectangle when I assign it to the `COLOR`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Make a canvas shader.\n- Assign it to a control as a Shader Material.\n- Add a uniform for the screen texture with hint_screen_texture and any of the filtering modes that end with _mipmap.\n- In the fragment do `COLOR = textureLod(screen_texture, UV, 2.0).rgb` and you get a black rectangle.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe expected behavior is the white rectangle should be blurred behind the shader. If you load the project in 4.2.dev1 or higher you will get a black rectangle instead. Keep in mind this only breaks when it is in Web on MacOS so you should test it in the web editor.\n\n[mipmapbug_2025-07-15_00-52-46.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21225835/mipmapbug_2025-07-15_00-52-46.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fa